<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Todd Lake Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:264-4: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.999772" lon="-121.663687"><ele>1935.4</ele><name>Dutchman Flat Sno-park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 559496151); confidence: high; pdf_page: 267; book_elev_ft: 6400; quote: map 60: DUTCHMAN FLAT NORDIC SNO-PARK 6400'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.009600" lon="-121.675900"><ele>1911.8</ele><name>Century Drive junction with the Todd Lake Trail (start of NF 360)</name><desc>source: OSM node where the meadow track (way 1467390216), the snow-covered Cascade Lakes Highway (way 1478886564, piste nordic) and NF 4600-360 (way 1486728088, in OSM route 'Todd Lake') meet; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 266; quote: ski north into the meadow, take the first trail fork to the left, and proceed to the Century Drive junction with the Todd Lake Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.017900" lon="-121.684200"><ele>1871.6</ele><name>Leave the road: Todd Lake Trail into the trees</name><desc>source: OSM west end of NF 4600-360 (way 357558076) where the nordic Todd Lake path (way 669880387) turns north; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 266; quote: The trail eventually curves left, then goes down a short, curving turn before leaving the road. It turns right, into trees</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.024400" lon="-121.683500"><ele>1876.9</ele><name>Todd Lake, south end</name><desc>source: OSM start of the Todd Lake Trail loop (way 367545460) at the lake's south shore, after crossing Road 370 at the Todd Lake trailhead (way 559391676); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 266; book_elev_ft: 6120; quote: To reach the lake, cross Road 370 and follow the lake access road up a gentle grade to the lower end of the scenic basin</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Todd Lake Trail</name><desc>1. Dutchman Flat Sno-park -&gt; Century Drive junction with the Todd Lake Trail (start of NF 360): osm (medium), 1.27 mi | 2. Century Drive junction with the Todd Lake Trail (start of NF 360) -&gt; Leave the road: Todd Lake Trail into the trees: osm (high), 1.03 mi | 3. Leave the road: Todd Lake Trail into the trees -&gt; Todd Lake, south end: osm (high), 0.61 mi</desc>
